{"kind":"request","text":"AR-4: a room without an archive destination stops retrying. AR-3 (9184dd26): all four archivable grow-demo scopes fail with target-missing every hour at the AR-1 cap, about 98 DO requests an hour and 64 M work units per burst, for nothing. No destination is a definite answer, not a transient failure. Builder lane after PT-1.","body":{"conditions":"1. When the Directory has no repository row, or its row lacks archive journal, the archive pass ends disabled with next null (as pin disabled does): no deferred wake. 2. A later bind-repository act (or whatever act sets the destination) signals the archive wake again, so a room that binds a destination archives without a deploy. 3. Real unavailability (unreadable reply, timeout, destination mismatch after a bind) keeps the AR-1 backoff. 4. Named reds: a room without a destination sets no wake after one pass; binding one wakes it; an unreadable target still retries. 5. The review states the wake floor and requests per room per hour before and after (from AR-3: about 98 DO requests per hour on grow-demo, to 0). 6. Deploy to dap-grow with a rate read; the :35 burst must vanish.","target_head":"d910468d3dd996aca2f3a96be8996ae0f42441bf","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}